---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description: "Curriculum vitae of Mahan Balooei.",
	title: "CV",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<div class="mb-12 flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-y-2">
		<h1 class="title">CV</h1>
		<a
			class="cactus-link text-sm font-semibold"
			href="/cv/CV_Mahan_Balooei.pdf"
			rel="noreferrer"
			target="_blank"
		>
			Download PDF CV →
		</a>
	</div>

	<section>
		<h2 class="title text-accent mb-4 text-lg">Research Interests</h2>
		<ul class="marker:text-accent list-disc space-y-1.5 ps-5 text-sm" role="list">
			<li>Protein language models and foundation models</li>
			<li>Machine learning for biological data</li>
			<li>Variant-effect and pathogenicity prediction</li>
			<li>Computational genomics and multi-omics</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="mt-10">
		<h2 class="title text-accent mb-4 text-lg">Education</h2>
		<div class="space-y-6 text-sm">
			<div>
				<p class="font-semibold">University of Bologna — MSc in Bioinformatics</p>
				<p class="text-muted">Oct 2024 – Present</p>
				<p class="mt-1 font-semibold">MSc Thesis: Protein Language Models for Human Protein Variant Pathogenicity Prediction</p>
				<p class="text-muted mt-1">Supervisors: Castrense Savojardo · Pier Luigi Martelli · Matteo Manfredi</p>
				<p class="mt-1">
					Ongoing thesis on modernizing the E-SNPs&amp;GO framework for missense variant pathogenicity
					prediction through updated human variant datasets and contemporary protein language models.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<p class="font-semibold">Iran University of Medical Sciences — BSc in Medical Laboratory Sciences</p>
				<p class="text-muted">Sept 2019 – Jul 2023</p>
				<p class="mt-1">
					Relevant coursework: Molecular Diagnostics, Immunoassays, Clinical Chemistry, Haematology,
					Microbiology, Virology.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="mt-10">
		<h2 class="title text-accent mb-4 text-lg">Publications</h2>
		<div class="text-sm">
			<p>
				Farmani, S.<sup>*</sup>, Dehghanbanadaki, N.<sup>*</sup>,
				<strong class="text-global-text">Balooei, M.<sup>*</sup></strong>, Mehralitabar, H., Sabaghian,
				H., &amp; Naderi-Manesh, H. <em>Mechanism-based targeting of lactate dehydrogenase
				tetramerization by naturally derived compounds: A survey of molecular docking, molecular
				dynamics, and QSAR analysis.</em> <em>Computers in Biology and Medicine</em>, 197(Pt B),
				111000, 2025.{" "}
				<a
					class="cactus-link"
					href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.compbiomed.2025.111000"
					rel="noreferrer"
					target="_blank"
				>
					Paper →
				</a>
			</p>
			<p class="text-muted mt-1 text-xs"><sup>*</sup>These authors contributed equally.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="mt-10">
		<h2 class="title text-accent mb-4 text-lg">Research Experience</h2>
		<div class="space-y-8 text-sm">
			<div>
				<p class="font-semibold">Protein Language Model-Based Signal Peptide Prediction</p>
				<p class="text-muted">MSc Bioinformatics Project — Independently Implemented · Apr 2026</p>
				<p class="mt-1">
					Built an end-to-end eukaryotic signal-peptide prediction pipeline using high-confidence
					UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot annotations and MMseqs2-based redundancy reduction. Compared von
					Heijne PSWM, biochemical-feature SVM, CNN-BiLSTM, and ESM-2 embedding-based models,
					achieving F1 = 0.962 and MCC = 0.957 on a held-out benchmark with the ESM-2-based model.
					Also analyzed amino-acid composition, signal-peptide lengths, kingdom-specific bias, and
					cleavage-site motifs for biological interpretation.{" "}
					<a class="cactus-link" href="https://github.com/MahanBalooei/eukaryotic-signal-peptide-prediction" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">Code</a>
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<p class="font-semibold">Protein Domain and Functional Annotation Using HMMER and MMseqs2</p>
				<p class="text-muted">Feb – Mar 2026</p>
				<p class="mt-1">
					Built a protein-domain annotation workflow using profile HMMs, HMMER, and MMseqs2 for
					large-scale sequence classification. Compared profile-based and sequence-similarity-based
					workflows, achieving MCC = 0.997 and MCC = 0.991, respectively, and connected classical
					homology methods to remote homology detection and protein-family classification.{" "}
					<a class="cactus-link" href="https://github.com/MahanBalooei/HMM_KunitzDomain" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">Code</a>
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<p class="font-semibold">Computational Epigenomics Analysis of DNA Methylation (Illumina 450K)</p>
				<p class="text-muted">Jun – Jul 2025</p>
				<p class="mt-1">
					Conducted an R/Bioconductor workflow for Illumina 450K methylation analysis, including
					quality control, normalization, PCA-based batch-effect assessment, differential methylation
					analysis, and DMR identification.{" "}
					<a class="cactus-link" href="https://github.com/MahanBalooei/epigenetic-methylation-450k" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">Code</a>
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<p class="font-semibold">Chest X-Ray Pneumonia Detection via Transfer Learning</p>
				<p class="text-muted">Apr – May 2026</p>
				<p class="mt-1">
					Compared ResNet50, EfficientNetB0, and DenseNet-121 XRV under class imbalance, evaluating
					threshold selection, ensembling, test-time augmentation, and Grad-CAM interpretability.
					DenseNet-121 XRV performed best under the maximum-MCC strategy.{" "}
					<a class="cactus-link" href="https://github.com/MahanBalooei/chest-xray-pneumonia-detection" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">Code</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="mt-10">
		<h2 class="title text-accent mb-4 text-lg">Skills</h2>
		<div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
			<p><span class="font-semibold">Protein Bioinformatics:</span> ESM-2, protein representation learning, HMMER, MMseqs2, BLAST, UniProt, PDB, protein functional/domain annotation, sequence-function prediction.</p>
			<p><span class="font-semibold">Machine Learning &amp; Deep Learning:</span> PyTorch, scikit-learn, TensorFlow, SVMs, CNN-BiLSTM, transfer learning, representation learning, model evaluation, class-imbalance handling.</p>
			<p><span class="font-semibold">Functional Genomics &amp; Epigenomics:</span> R/Bioconductor, minfi, Illumina 450K methylation analysis, differential methylation, PCA-based batch-effect assessment.</p>
			<p><span class="font-semibold">Research Computing:</span> Python, R, Bash/Linux, SQL, Git/GitHub, Docker, HPC/Slurm, conda, Jupyter Notebooks.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

